      <p class="_abstract">When using the <code>cluster-compare</code> plugin, you might see unexpected results, such as false positives or conflicts when multiple cluster custom resources (CRs) exist.</p>
      <h2 id="troubleshooting-cc-false-positives_troubleshooting-cluster-comparisons" class="group scroll-mt-20">Troubleshooting false positives for missing resources<a href="#troubleshooting-cc-false-positives_troubleshooting-cluster-comparisons" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h2>
      <p class="_abstract">The plugin might report a missing resource even though the cluster custom resource (CR) is present in the cluster.</p>
      <p><strong>Procedure</strong></p>
      <ol>
      <li>Ensure you are using the latest version of the <code>cluster-compare</code> plugin. For more information, see "Installing the cluster-compare plugin".</li>
      <li>Ensure you are using the most up-to-date version of the reference configuration.</li>
      <li>Ensure that template has the same <code>apiVersion</code>, <code>kind</code>, <code>name</code>, and <code>namespace</code> fields as the cluster CR.</li>
      </ol>
